# Review ownership for the paths where a mistake is expensive.
#
# GitHub matches the LAST pattern that fits, so the specific rules sit below the
# catch-all. This file only REQUESTS a reviewer — enforcing it (and blocking a
# merge without the review) is the "Require review from Code Owners" branch
# protection setting, which lives in the repository, not here.
#
# Keep it short: every line here is a claim that somebody must look at that
# change. A file that lists everything protects nothing.

# Default: the maintainer reviews everything.
* @XIIIMICT

# Applied migrations are immutable and a wrong one cannot be undone on a stand
# that already ran it — DROP COLUMN in production has no rollback.
/back/migrations/ @XIIIMICT

# The schema itself: a model change without a matching migration is the most
# common way a deploy breaks an existing installation.
/back/src/collab/models.py @XIIIMICT
/back/src/auth/models.py @XIIIMICT

# Wiring that decides who may read what, and how the outside world is trusted.
/back/src/auth/ @XIIIMICT
/back/src/config.py @XIIIMICT
/back/src/main.py @XIIIMICT

# The CI contract: a change here can turn a broken build green.
/.github/ @XIIIMICT

# Deployment: compose profiles, images and the reverse-proxy contract.
/compose.yaml @XIIIMICT
/infra/ @XIIIMICT
